      "content_json": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "Why",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "On 2026-10-15 three mirror workers bootstrapped the same new 7 GB GitHub mirror at once. Two GitHub pushes arrived during the first bootstrap, and nothing stops a second worker from syncing a target that is already in sync. The losing pushes left about 63 GB of duplicate packs, and concurrent indexing took prod nodes to 61 of 61.9 GB of Go memory.",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "The same race happens on small repos all the time: 39k raced syncs and 33k leaked packs in the 15 days to 2026-10-15.",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "What",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "A Proposed ADR, ",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "text": "docs/adrs/20261016-mirror-sync-target-lease.md",
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": ". The change it describes is in mirror-pipeline and fleet, not in entiredb.",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "bulletList",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "text": "A worker holds a lease on the target repo, in a new JetStream KV bucket ",
                        "type": "text"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "mirror_sync_leases",
                        "type": "text",
                        "marks": [
                          {
                            "type": "code"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", while it syncs.",
                        "type": "text"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "text": "The lease has a 45 min bucket TTL and no renewal. It outlives the 30 min sync budget.",
                        "type": "text"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "text": "A job that finds the lease held writes a pending note per source kind into the lease and acks. The holder republishes the notes as fresh jobs before its own Ack, Nak or Term.",
                        "type": "text"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "text": "A redelivery of the holder's own job, or a lease older than the sync budget, takes over the lease. A holder that lost its lease steps aside.",
                        "type": "text"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "text": "One lease covers all source kinds, because a GitHub sync and a namespace sync both send the full history to an empty target.",
                        "type": "text"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "The ADR also lists the rejected alternatives and one open question.",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "Verification",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "Docs only. ",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "text": "git diff --check",
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
